eparator` helper. Its logic is unchanged: `'/'` is always flagged, and on Windows a `\\` is flagged only if the pattern is an existing directory.\n- `--full-path` still turns the check off for every pattern.\n\n**Tests (`tests/tests.rs`):**\n- `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`: a `/` in an `--and` pattern produces the error, including when the bad pattern is second of two `--and` patterns.\n- `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_allowed_with_full_path`: with `--full-path`, an `--and` pattern containing `/` is accepted and matches. This test doesn't run on Windows, same as the existing primary-pattern test.\n\nI haven't committed anything.","ttft_ms":2437,"type":"result","duration_ms":103282,"uuid":"bbc38b77-9e99-4de9-80e2-4b42a63b7e95","ttft_stream_ms":1101,"time_to_request_ms":134,"first_content_frame_ms":1101,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
